diff --git a/docs/docs/defaults.md b/docs/docs/defaults.md
index 60772fa..57bf256 100644
--- a/docs/docs/defaults.md
+++ b/docs/docs/defaults.md
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-With *defaults* it is possible to configure implicit default settings for interfaces. The `match:` option is a filter to select on which interfaces the defaults should be applied. Only the defaults of the first match are applied. There are several [*clear_…* settings](../schema/{{ ifstate_branch }}/#defaults_items) which allows clearing interface settings blocks (*addresses*, *fdb*, …).
+With *defaults* it is possible to configure implicit default settings for interfaces. The `match:` option is a filter to select on which interfaces the defaults should be applied. The settings of all matching entries are merged: if more than one entry sets the same option, the first one wins, also within `link:` and `ethtool:`. There are several [*clear_…* settings](../schema/{{ ifstate_branch }}/#defaults_items) which allows clearing interface settings blocks (*addresses*, *fdb*, …).
 
 [Schema description](/schema/{{ ifstate_branch }}/#defaults)
 
@@ -9,15 +9,14 @@ parameters:
     - match:
         # regex matching on interface name
         - ifname: '^HA$'
-      # remove any ip addresses if an interface has no `addresses:` setting
-      clear_addresses: true
+      # keep any ip addresses if an interface has no `addresses:` setting
+      clear_addresses: false
       # add some implicit link settings
       link:
-        state: down
         ifalias: ''
 ```
 
-There is also an implicit builtin `defaults_builtin` setting which clears settings not specified in the `interfaces` settings:
+There is also an implicit builtin `defaults_builtin` setting which clears settings not specified in the `interfaces` settings. It matches every interface and has the lowest precedence, so any matching entry in `defaults` overrides its settings:
 
 ```yaml
 parameters:
@@ -39,4 +38,8 @@ parameters:
     The implicit cleanup since ifstate 2.0 differse from the behavior of ifstate 1.x,
     where unspecified settings were just ignored.
 
+!!! warning "Breaking Change"
+
+    Up to ifstate 2.5 only the first matching entry was applied, so an entry in `defaults` replaced the builtin defaults for the interfaces it matched. See [Upgrades](upgrades.md) for details.
+
 These built-in entries can be viewed with the `ìfstatecli showall` action.
diff --git a/docs/docs/upgrades.md b/docs/docs/upgrades.md
index 4967ed6..541de84 100644
--- a/docs/docs/upgrades.md
+++ b/docs/docs/upgrades.md
@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@
 This site summarizes **breaking changes** you should consider when upgrading between major releases. You should also check the [ChangeLog](../changelog.md) for a complete list of changes.
 
+## IfState 2.6
+
+### Merged defaults
+
+Up to IfState 2.5 only the first matching entry of [`parameters.defaults`](defaults.md) was applied, so the builtin defaults were skipped for any interface matching an entry in `defaults`. IfState now merges all matching entries: a setting an entry leaves out is taken from the next matching entry, and finally from the builtin defaults. An entry that relied on leaving out a *clear_…* setting now has to set it to `false`, and the builtin link settings `state: down` and `master: null` now apply unless the interface or an entry sets them.
+
 ## IfState 2.4
 
 ### ethtool Feature Names
